WEBVTT

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.409
[engine revs]

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:14.948
[Jerry] <i>This is a 1967 Austin-Healey 3000</i>
<i>in ice blue.</i>

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.820
<i>It has a straight-six,</i>
<i>150-horsepower engine.</i>

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:25.192
<i>This is a car if you wanna say,</i>
<i>"I really love British sports cars.</i>

00:00:25.259 --> 00:00:27.895
<i>"And damn it, I will go down</i>
<i>with that ship if I have to."</i>

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.033
<i>-Hello?</i>
<i>-Ricky?</i>

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.267
<i>-Who's that?</i>
<i>-Jerry.</i>

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:35.333
[Ricky] <i>Hello, man.</i>

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.537
<i>-How's it going?</i>
<i>-</i>[Jerry] <i>What are you doing?</i>

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.107
[Ricky]<i> Oh. Sitting out, I think I've got</i>
<i>irritable bowel syndrome.</i>

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.767
[Jerry] <i>Oh, God, that is irritating.</i>

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.077
[Ricky laughs] Yeah.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.946
-[Jerry] <i>You wanna grab a coffee?</i>
-<i>Yeah.</i>

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:53.921
<i>I'm Jerry Seinfeld, and this is</i>
Comedians in Cars Getting Coffee.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:56.733
<i>Today my guest is my good friend</i>
<i>Ricky Gervais.</i>

00:00:56.967 --> 00:00:59.767
<i>He's a very funny, silly,</i>
<i>English comedian guy.</i>

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:00.800
[laughs]

00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:02.867
[Jerry]
<i>And he's just funny. He makes me laugh.</i>

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.398
-What do you think?
-[Ricky] It's great.

00:01:05.132 --> 00:01:06.900
-English.
-Is it?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.867
-Is it?
-I don't know anything.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.238
-You don't know anything about cars?
-No.

00:01:12.873 --> 00:01:14.508
-Is this the seat belt?
-What do you think so far?

00:01:14.575 --> 00:01:16.843
-I think it's a death trap.
-It is.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:20.300
There's no way there's a little air bag
in there, is there?

00:01:20.681 --> 00:01:23.817
-There is, but you have to blow it up.
-[laughing]

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.800
Quick, we're gonna crash.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.588
Right.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.060
Well, I'm a very nervous passenger,
so let's...

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.333
-Did you eat?
-I had some cereal.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.966
-That's so sweet.
-What?

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.400
What kind of cereal?

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:44.133
We can't be running out
of stuff to talk about already.

00:01:44.371 --> 00:01:46.707
If we're going into detail on the cereal,

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:48.633
we're struggling.

00:01:51.178 --> 00:01:52.813
There's a dancing traffic cop.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.167
He's dancing, he's really
having a good time.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:56.950
She's dancing, too.

00:01:58.185 --> 00:01:59.620
We're in the middle of <i>Fame.</i>

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:02.100
Irene Cara.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.967
Irene Cara.
She did the song, didn't she?

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.433
Yes, <i>Fame</i>.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.233
I'm gonna live forever.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.997
-I'm gonna learn how to fly.
-Yeah.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.933
People are gonna see me and die.
Well, who's gonna pay for that?

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.000
I think they meant it in a sort of...

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:18.833
-I saw Irene Cara, I died.
-Ah, I see.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.800
-Yeah, exactly.
-In a more like this way.

00:02:20.867 --> 00:02:22.533
-I died.
-I died.

00:02:22.576 --> 00:02:23.477
-Yeah.
-I see.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.500
Look at this guy.

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:30.984
Nobody can explain
why the homeless have such fabulous hair.

00:02:31.051 --> 00:02:33.353
I love how you start
with "no one can explain."

00:02:33.433 --> 00:02:37.200
Like scientists have been working
around the clock for the last 25 years.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:39.267
They've spent billions
of government dollars,

00:02:39.326 --> 00:02:40.861
but they've not come up with anything.

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.463
Like, who commissioned
this scientific study?

00:02:45.433 --> 00:02:47.033
Okay, here we go.

00:02:47.134 --> 00:02:48.201
[engine revving]

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.167
No, be sensible.

00:02:51.805 --> 00:02:52.806
[Jerry] Oh, Jerry.

00:02:54.141 --> 00:02:55.042
Jesus.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.510
Sorry,

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.011
are we in <i>The Italian Job?</i>

00:02:58.078 --> 00:02:59.279
Why are we doing this?

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.267
Oh, no, that made it worse. You--

00:03:02.716 --> 00:03:05.252
Jerry! For [bleep] sake!

00:03:05.686 --> 00:03:07.954
We're going 70 miles an hour.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.200
We're not going 70.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:12.700
[Ricky] Let's take the bus.

00:03:14.233 --> 00:03:15.133
[Jerry] Oh, Jerry.

00:03:16.263 --> 00:03:17.164
Oh, God.

00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:22.367
Jerry, why is it so funny
to frighten a grown man?

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:24.800
Fear is funny.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:28.141
-Fear is funny, yeah.
-Especially when it's not fake.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:31.478
We're so used to fake fear.
Everyone always acts scared,

00:03:31.545 --> 00:03:33.580
-pretends their scared.
-This is real, don't worry about it.

00:03:33.647 --> 00:03:36.183
I'm in a tin bucket with no suspension.

00:03:37.017 --> 00:03:38.185
Oh, Jesus.

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.187
When was the last time
you were this scared?

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:43.223
Doing award shows
and potentially ending my career is my...

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:45.425
That's my adrenaline rush.

00:03:45.492 --> 00:03:47.661
I work for the Golden Globe committee.

00:03:48.929 --> 00:03:52.632
And this entire thing is a ruse
to get you to do the show again next year.

00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:53.733
Yeah.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.533
And I'm just gonna keep driving you
in this terrifying car until you agree.

00:03:58.567 --> 00:03:59.800
Oh, God.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.467
I think the first couple,
they were sort of...

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.567
They were taken aback.

00:04:06.233 --> 00:04:10.133
"Why is this Brit saying
all these awful things to us?"

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:14.867
And then by the third one,
they go, "He's telling jokes. I get it."

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.600
What was the introduction for Mel Gibson?

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.533
"I like a drink as much as the next man.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.467
"Unless the next man is Mel Gibson."

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:24.500
That's a great joke.

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.833
I like a joke that
sneaks up on you like that.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:31.538
Yeah. Oh, Jesus Christ! Ow!

00:04:31.605 --> 00:04:34.174
I can't understand
why this company went out of business

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:36.467
shortly after this car was made.

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:39.633
You really are holding on seriously there.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.533
[Ricky] Yeah.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.667
It feels like I'm being dragged along
in a tin bath.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.500
That's what this feels like.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:52.192
Oh, God, you have to turn around
like an owl to see.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.961
There's no mirror in this car.

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.429
Jerry, you can't...

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.366
There's a mirror here.
I see exactly what I'm doing.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:02.233
-Oh, Christ.
-[Jerry] What are you worried about?

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:03.236
[Ricky] What am I worried about?

00:05:05.272 --> 00:05:08.375
I was thinking maybe for the drive back,
we'd put the top down.

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:10.010
Whatever.

00:05:10.911 --> 00:05:12.479
For [bleep] sake.

00:05:12.546 --> 00:05:14.281
Oh, come on, Jerry, this is mental.

00:05:14.381 --> 00:05:17.484
You don't need to do this.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:20.020
We're going for coffee, for Christ's sake.

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:22.900
We're not going to diffuse a bomb, right?

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.667
There's no need for this.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.600
Even Jack Bauer had an hour, right?

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.565
It's turned into a race now.

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:35.168
-It's like a scene from <i>Ronin.</i>
<i></i>-[laughing]

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.767
That was a good laugh to start the day.

00:05:38.233 --> 00:05:40.900
My pain and suffering is
for everyone else.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.233
-I fall over for your amusement.
-Yes. Yes. Yes.

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:45.133
-Of course.
-Now you got it.

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:47.633
If someone's laughing with me or at me,
I've done my job.

00:05:47.681 --> 00:05:48.682
-That's right.
-Yeah.

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:55.733
[Jerry] The funniest thing
about the nervous passenger is

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:59.326
that you think that that hand
could possibly do something.

00:05:59.426 --> 00:06:00.293
I know, yeah.

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:03.200
Jesus Christ! And I'm an atheist.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:14.307
If you weren't a part of, arguably,
the most successful sitcom of all time...

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.600
Why is it arguable? What's the argument?

00:06:17.177 --> 00:06:19.312
And who's arguing on the other side,
I wanna know.

00:06:20.867 --> 00:06:23.767
If you weren't as successful as you are...

00:06:23.833 --> 00:06:24.933
Yeah?

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:28.767
Rich, famous, loved, okay?

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:30.867
Please, go on.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:34.127
You'd seem a bit like a maniac now.

00:06:34.194 --> 00:06:38.231
This is what mad people do,
drive and giggle at people's fear.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.100
"Jerry Seinfeld wants you to do his show.
It's called...

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:44.067
<i>Couple of Comedians Going</i>
<i>for a Drive for Coffee. </i>"Oh, great."

00:06:44.333 --> 00:06:47.567
"A man wants to drive you around New York
really fast

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:50.143
in a death machine, laughing."

00:06:56.049 --> 00:06:57.984
Look at this, Ricky.
"Welcome to City Island."

00:06:58.533 --> 00:07:01.067
-Look at the nautical environment.
-Yeah. Lovely.

00:07:01.133 --> 00:07:03.067
-This is great. Come on.
-Yeah.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.367
We've never been here.

00:07:04.491 --> 00:07:07.060
You would never ever come here
if it wasn't for me.

00:07:07.127 --> 00:07:08.128
No.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:11.331
I'm giving you a gift.
And I'm going to let you live, as well.

00:07:11.398 --> 00:07:14.067
-You've given me the gift of life.
-The gift of life.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.538
Look at this.

00:07:18.972 --> 00:07:21.207
I can see sort of an '80s film starting
like this...

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:24.210
Where a writer comes
and then he gets embroiled.

00:07:25.345 --> 00:07:27.414
Oh, I love when someone gets embroiled.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.616
I love people getting embroiled.

00:07:29.733 --> 00:07:31.200
They shouldn't have been embroiled.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.633
I'm going to a fishing village
and the first thing that happens is...

00:07:33.933 --> 00:07:34.767
They get embroiled.

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:35.755
They get embroiled.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:39.926
And the reason people get embroiled is,
you never see the embroiling coming.

00:07:39.993 --> 00:07:40.994
No.

00:07:41.061 --> 00:07:43.296
You never can you see that
I'm about to get embroiled.

00:07:43.363 --> 00:07:44.397
[laughing]

00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:50.837
If you were in the electric chair,
they would ask you,

00:07:50.904 --> 00:07:52.272
"Do you have any last words?"

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:54.841
How could you beat Gary Gilmore?

00:07:55.275 --> 00:07:58.044
His last words were, "Let's do it."

00:07:58.144 --> 00:07:59.145
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:03.717
I really think the death penalty's
too depressing to even think about.

00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:05.118
I don't...

00:08:05.767 --> 00:08:08.067
I mean, I don't agree with it.

00:08:08.167 --> 00:08:11.800
The state can show
that sort of form of violence.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.967
What about abortion?
Do you agree with that?

00:08:14.027 --> 00:08:15.595
Yeah, but that's different, isn't it?

00:08:16.029 --> 00:08:19.833
I guess you can just arrange things
the way you like them.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:25.405
-When you're rich, famous, like you.
-Yeah.

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:27.140
Unlike you,

00:08:27.767 --> 00:08:31.000
who's just a guy with an old car

00:08:31.067 --> 00:08:34.267
going along the highway,
laughing maniacally

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.533
'cause someone feels they're about to die.

00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:41.600
I should have said "let's do it"
when I got in this car.

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:51.498
[steam hisses]

00:08:52.033 --> 00:08:53.333
[woman] You guys want coffee?

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:54.500
I would love some.

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:57.203
-Just a regular filtered coffee with milk.
-I'll have half and half.

00:09:01.533 --> 00:09:04.200
Could I have two yellow eggs
and two egg whites?

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:07.280
What do you mean by that?
You mean four eggs?

00:09:08.167 --> 00:09:11.133
-Two yolks and two whites.
-That's just two eggs.

00:09:11.184 --> 00:09:12.452
-That's four eggs.
-No.

00:09:12.519 --> 00:09:15.455
Two yolks and two whites is two eggs.
What do you mean?

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:21.294
-Two additional whites on top of--
-Right, so four whites and two yolks.

00:09:21.728 --> 00:09:23.063
-That's correct.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:26.633
You're like a young king, aren't you?
Things are kept from you.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.435
But you wanna do stuff.

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:30.770
They go,
"He wants to drive around in a car."

00:09:31.271 --> 00:09:33.840
And someone said, "Well, just let him
drive around in the car."

00:09:33.907 --> 00:09:36.509
-"No, he wants to do it with celebrities."
-"He wants to do it

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.067
with some friends he's seen
on the telly."

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.300
"Well, get their number."

00:09:40.767 --> 00:09:42.800
Would you like some jelly for your toast?

00:09:42.849 --> 00:09:44.851
[Ricky] No, I'm fine.
That's great, thank you.

00:09:51.267 --> 00:09:52.567
-How was your--
-How were your eggs?

00:09:57.664 --> 00:09:59.365
What are these guys doing here?

00:10:03.436 --> 00:10:04.370
It's Tuesday...

00:10:05.738 --> 00:10:06.840
at 11 o' clock.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:08.733
Who do you think you are?

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.067
You could be a good...

00:10:11.411 --> 00:10:15.081
lt's like a man strolling into town going,
"I want to find out what you're doing.

00:10:15.215 --> 00:10:16.416
"Just reading the paper."

00:10:16.633 --> 00:10:18.333
Make sure he's just read the paper.

00:10:19.367 --> 00:10:20.633
See you later.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:25.767
Although, the older I get...

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.100
the more annoyed I am

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:30.233
by what I call...

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:31.967
"other people."

00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:35.702
There are people walking around. I'm
going, "Why are you scuffling your feet?

00:10:35.767 --> 00:10:37.100
There's no one to pick your feet up.

00:10:37.167 --> 00:10:40.100
Don't walk around with your jaw open.
Why do you eat chewing gum like that?

00:10:40.167 --> 00:10:42.400
Don't sniff that loudly in public.

00:10:42.567 --> 00:10:44.167
Don't spit on the floor."

00:10:44.233 --> 00:10:46.633
-Right, you might like Singapore.
-Why do you say that?

00:10:46.733 --> 00:10:48.800
-They take care of that stuff.
-Do they really?

00:10:48.848 --> 00:10:50.383
-Oh, yeah...
-There's etiquette police

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:53.019
Yeah, you spit your gum on the street,
it's 50 lashes.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.156
Okay, that's going too far, isn't it?

00:10:56.222 --> 00:10:58.958
I don't think so.
Not if you really want it clean.

00:11:00.533 --> 00:11:02.967
Is that kosher?
You just had bacon.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.400
Slap the cuffs on, judge.

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:10.567
-You got me.
-Listen, I don't make the rules.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.933
You want to, you said before,

00:11:12.972 --> 00:11:14.641
you want to be the mayor
that goes around and says,

00:11:14.707 --> 00:11:17.210
"Shut your mouth,
stop chewing your gum like that

00:11:17.277 --> 00:11:19.279
-and quit shuffling your feet."
-Yeah.

00:11:23.267 --> 00:11:27.800
What is the moment in history
that you would like to witness in person?

00:11:27.921 --> 00:11:30.123
I'll tell you mine just
to get the conversation rolling.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.267
-Okay.
-Gettysburg Address.

00:11:32.325 --> 00:11:35.228
I would like to have been in that crowd
and heard the Gettysburg Address.

00:11:35.962 --> 00:11:38.731
Churchill? Would you like to be there
when he's crafting a speech?

00:11:38.798 --> 00:11:42.502
How about being in Hitler's bunker
there as he's screaming?

00:11:42.569 --> 00:11:45.471
I'd be a bit nervous,
but then, after that car journey,

00:11:45.538 --> 00:11:48.374
Hitler doesn't scare me as much.
I'll be honest.

00:11:50.009 --> 00:11:51.344
[Ricky] Thank you.

00:11:51.411 --> 00:11:54.280
On the last day,
the Russians were advancing.

00:11:54.347 --> 00:11:57.483
They were 200 yards down the road.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.252
He married Eva Braun, right?

00:11:59.319 --> 00:12:02.522
They had ordered cake and some champagne.

00:12:02.889 --> 00:12:04.857
They retired to bed early.

00:12:04.967 --> 00:12:06.533
In the morning,

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:11.200
he poisoned her and shot himself.

00:12:11.333 --> 00:12:14.200
And the gardener burned the bodies, right?

00:12:14.267 --> 00:12:16.269
-Now, say what you will about Hitler...
-Yeah.

00:12:16.336 --> 00:12:19.272
But that's a terrible honeymoon, isn't it?
That's a crap honeymoon.

00:12:22.709 --> 00:12:25.945
The funniest part of that joke is,
"Say what you will about Hitler."

00:12:29.549 --> 00:12:32.185
I'm gonna go to the toilet
and take a Valium for the journey back.

00:12:32.252 --> 00:12:33.286
[laughing]

00:12:33.367 --> 00:12:34.867
If that's okay.

00:12:36.923 --> 00:12:38.891
[engine revving]

00:12:41.794 --> 00:12:44.264
[laughing]

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.365
Right. Okay.

00:12:59.012 --> 00:13:00.580
[laughs]

00:13:01.547 --> 00:13:04.751
Jesus, this is like free falling.

00:13:04.817 --> 00:13:07.320
I know, it's fantastic.
Don't you feel alive?

00:13:07.387 --> 00:13:08.688
Yeah.

00:13:08.755 --> 00:13:10.923
-Even if only for a few more minutes.
-Shut up!

00:13:12.492 --> 00:13:15.928
[Jerry] I bet you this car looks great.
I'm in heaven.

00:13:17.167 --> 00:13:18.833
Do you think we look gay?

00:13:18.931 --> 00:13:20.333
The least of my worries.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.536
We're in stylish sunglasses,
we got the top down...

00:13:23.603 --> 00:13:25.305
-Yeah.
-in a poncy roadster.

00:13:25.371 --> 00:13:27.106
-Yeah.
-I think we look gay.

00:13:27.173 --> 00:13:30.310
I can just imagine you saying that
when our parachutes didn't open.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.945
And I'm all nervous.

00:13:33.279 --> 00:13:37.016
You think we look gay?
It doesn't matter... it doesn't matter.

00:13:37.083 --> 00:13:39.285
[laughing]

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.455
[Jerry continues laughing]

00:13:42.522 --> 00:13:44.257
[Ricky] I'm never gonna do this again.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.893
[Jerry cackles]

00:13:47.533 --> 00:13:48.800
[Ricky] Whoa, what the [bleep]